cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Cellular Inference Mesh: Salabim discrete-event simulation of edge-cloud LLM inference under PACELC saturation"
abstract: >
  Discrete-event simulation in Salabim of the Cellular Inference Mesh edge-cloud
  architecture for industrial multilingual AGV voice command processing under PACELC.
  Implements 300 Monte-Carlo replicates × 3 scenarios × 2 arms × 1800 simulated
  seconds with parametric variation per replicate. Verifies the Theorem
  (Pareto-efficiency over 5 axes against 256 sub-compositions and 7 external
  architectures) and articulates the Saturated Pipeline Conjecture, which
  explains the structural insensitivity of percentile-99 latency to fallback-rate
  reductions under edge saturation. Reproducibility guaranteed via SHA-256 hash
  chain and bit-parity tests.
